## Scientific narrative (current — do not revert to K=4-only story)

The paper has **two linked tracks**. State both clearly; never conflate them.

### Track 1 — Cross-laboratory holdout (headline claim)

- **Scope:** Joint population training, leave-mice-out, 20 HQ mice, labs 2/3/5, K=3 macro ladder.
- **Headline:** cHMM–GMVAE mean prior NMI **~0.58** vs cGMVAE **~0.28** on joint holdout (Table 1).
- **Role:** Establishes zero-shot staging without subject ID or per-mouse calibration.
- **Limitation to name inline:** REM recall ~3% on strict holdout (S3 Fig); fold 2 / lab 2 heterogeneity.

### Track 2 — Substage biology (scientific payoff)

Expert Wake, NREM, and REM are a **reference partition for NMI**, not the hypothesis that sleep has only three regimes.

| Sweep | Scope | What it shows | Use in text |
|-------|-------|---------------|-------------|
| **Holdout fold 4** | Six held-out mice | Macro NMI peaks near K=3–4; declines at higher K; log-likelihood rises | **Generalisation benchmark** — underpowered for naming substages at K≥6 |
| **Population** | All 20 mice, same locked recipe | Cleaner latent separation; physiology panels at **K=6** (Figs 4–5), PCA at K=6/9/12 (Fig 3) | **Biology and naming** — not used to pick K for the holdout claim |

**K selection rule (state in Methods + Results):** When macro NMI and prior log-density diverge, choose mixture count for **interpretable physiology** in the **~7–9 substage** range (light vs deep NREM, active vs quiet Wake, boundary bouts, artefact buckets) — **not** at the macro-NMI peak alone.

### Biological reading at K=6 (population sweep — main Figs 4–5)

Use these names when writing Results; numbers from Figs 4–5 and Table S15 context:

| State | Role | Notes for prose |
|-------|------|-----------------|
| **S2** | Core quiet Wake | ~36% occupancy, ~98% expert Wake, long bouts |
| **S5, S6** | Dominant NREM substates | ~21% / ~19%, ~92% expert NREM, N2-/N3-like depth in spectra |
| **S3** | Consolidated REM | ~6%, ~66% expert REM — model **does not** split REM further even at K=12 |
| **S1, S4** | Boundary substates | Short bouts, Wake–NREM mixing, appear as brief hypnogram excursions |

After merging boundary buckets S1 and S4, the parsimonious map is **two Wake, two NREM, one REM** — aligned with the ~7–9 target when transition states are collapsed.

**Consistent reviewer finding:** The model subdivides **Wake and NREM** more readily than **REM** (phasic vs tonic). Say this plainly; cite mcRBM/thesis parallel in one sentence.

**EMG line artefacts:** Narrowband ~28 Hz and ~50 Hz peaks in substage spectra are acquisition artefacts from unshielded headstage wiring on the European mains grid — not sleep-related muscle tone. Mention when discussing physiology (Fig 4, S16 Fig).

### What not to claim

- Do **not** present K=4 holdout as the substage discovery result.
- Do **not** use K=13 fold-4 taxonomy as a main figure without labeling it illustrative / SI-only.
- Do **not** treat population NMI as comparable to holdout NMI without stating the scope change.

