## Quality checklist before hand-in

- [ ] Abstract has **zero parentheses** and ≤250 words.
- [ ] Main text scanned for `;` and excess `(` — split into sentences.
- [ ] Two-track substage story explicit — holdout generalisation vs population biology.
- [ ] K=6 biological names used consistently — S2 Wake, S5/S6 NREM, S3 REM, S1/S4 boundary.
- [ ] REM failure and “no REM split” stated in Results, not only SI.
- [ ] Every figure cited before it appears; panels match narrative.
- [ ] Holdout protocol in Methods **and** Fig 1.
- [ ] Limitations name — label noise, lab heterogeneity, seed fragility, fold-4 underpowering for K≥6, REM recall.
- [ ] No placeholder / thesis-arc / repo-path language in PDF.
- [ ] `texcount` main text ≤ 4,000; target 3,000–3,500 ([`word_budget.md`](docs/paper/notes/word_budget.md))
